        contentEn: "1. A record shall be made of formal statements made by any person who is questioned in connection with an investigation or with proceedings. The record shall be signed by the person who records and conducts the questioning and by the person who is questioned and his or her counsel, if present, and, where applicable, the Prosecutor or the judge who is present. The record shall note the date, time and place of the questioning.\n2. Any reservations that the person questioned may have regarding the content of the record shall be noted in the record."
